Miniforge*.sh
Miniconda*.sh

# Same bug pattern found in Project 3: Project 2's retriever creates a
# Chroma client during os.chdir() (correctly pointed at Project 2's real
# index), but a later .search() call happens after cwd is restored --
# if Chroma re-resolves any relative path at query time (not just
# client-creation time), it can write a stray, duplicate index HERE
# instead of using Project 2's real one. This line prevents that from
# being accidentally committed if it recurs.
data/chroma_db/
